# L §5.16 Pins (current text): "The pinned expression is evaluated unpinned; a hole pins the hole (§5.11)"; L §5.11:
# "A value or sample pin whose value is a hole pins that hole". The uniform hu has no row: the sample of emp is that
# hole on every path, and so is the mean. (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.16 when the text said "must be known".)
# (Writer 8: empirical is gone (L §2.3); emp is now discrete(eq[k] for k in ks), eq = 1 at both keys, and its
# value is read as ev = vals[emp], the form L §5.16 gives for "one of n known values drawn with equal weight",
# e[discrete(1 for k in IDX)]: the same uniforms, and the samples 0 and 2 as before, emp itself now ka or kb.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index ks = [ka, kb]
input w[k in ks]: num
input vals[k in ks]: num
input eq[k in ks]: num
input q25: num
input neg: num
input y1: num
input hu: num
def draw: dist = discrete(w[k] for k in ks) at reader
def emp: dist = discrete(eq[k] for k in ks) at reader
def ev: num = vals[emp] at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  w[ka] = 1
  w[kb] = 1
  vals[ka] = 0
  vals[kb] = 2
  eq[*] = 1
  q25 = 0.25
  neg = -1
  y1 = 1

ask a: mean(ev) with sample emp.u = hu law 2026-06-30 paths 2 seed 3
=== expect
a: ?"hu: no value at 2026-06-30" (hu)
  pinned sample: emp.u = ?"hu: no value at 2026-06-30" (hu)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
